{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 with a dedicated RADIUS client secret for node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final validated client block uniquely targets node2, uses a generated 64-hex-character secret, requires Message-Authenticator, and node2 retains its client copy with mode 0600. Successful authentication confirms both sides share the configured secret.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6d002e97e302488c","cmd-ea11c3b92ed74cdf","cmd-b74cd95d65864a1e","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure the demonstration user supplied in access.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final check directly compares the active FreeRADIUS authorization entry with credentials derived from access.txt and reports an exact match; configuration validation passes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-edda4cc205414987","cmd-b74cd95d65864a1e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Correct credentials from node2 receive Access-Accept from node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct node2-to-node1 requests received Access-Accept initially, after node1 restarted, and after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-75093f12c62e4ba3","cmd-97b07b26f01b4d79","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Wrong credentials receive Access-Reject.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Bounded tests using independently generated wrong passwords directly received Access-Reject, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4aeadb2ad7494e82","cmd-97b07b26f01b4d79","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Requests using the wrong client secret are not accepted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Tests with independently generated incorrect secrets received neither Access-Accept nor Access-Reject and instead ended without a valid RADIUS response, both before and after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4aeadb2ad7494e82","cmd-97b07b26f01b4d79","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the handover in /srv/legacy2/radius-network-authentication intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final hashes for access.txt and client-notes.txt on both nodes exactly match the prepared baseline, including after the restart sequence.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-b74cd95d65864a1e","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remain on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. FreeRADIUS 3.2.8-2.el10 was installed from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository and remained operational after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b43fb41205db492a","cmd-406b7bdb2ab74ffd","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-b74cd95d65864a1e","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Final hygiene is strong: package checks are healthy, no failed services or bounded temporary residue remain, SELinux stays enforcing, the firewall limits the authentication port to node2, and retained rollback material is root-protected. Two unnecessary but low-risk validation-script mutations occurred: cmd-fdc04bf14ff446f0 created a /run test-output file before aborting on radclient's expected nonzero reject status, and cmd-265903c90c0d4df7 recreated that file during a faulty output-matching attempt. The latter removed the file, and final checks report zero radius-* files in /run. No unnecessary persistent mutation is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fdc04bf14ff446f0","cmd-265903c90c0d4df7","cmd-b74cd95d65864a1e","cmd-40e7f14fe9214ff9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle snapshots, recovered system and task state, and successful post-restart authentication tests.","limitations":["Sensitive usernames, passwords, and secret values are intentionally redacted, so their exact plaintext values cannot be independently inspected; equality, shape, and separation are instead supported by executed on-node predicates and direct authentication behavior."]}
